/* book exam traps: Pseudorange is not the geometric range. It carries the receiver clock offset and the propagation delays; writing ρ = r as if the clocks were perfect throws away the reason for the fourth satellite. | Do not mix the carrier with the code. L1 is 1575.42 MHz; the C/A chip rate is 1.023 Mchip/s, exactly 1/1540 of it. One C/A chip is about 293 m, one L1 cycle only 0.19 m. | DOP is geometry, not an error source. It multiplies the range error; it cannot create one, and a low DOP cannot rescue a biased pseudorange. */
